-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Concept 1 :

OUTBOX PATTERN USE CASE :  Inconsistent state

Suppose : User hits - > Post : /upload/

Step 1 : Video saved       ✅
Step 2 : Metadata saved    ✅
Step 3 : Kafka crashed     ❌

DB Status = UPLOADED but Processing Service didn't received so Video Forever Status Stucked = UPLOADED


Resolution :

Save Video

↓

Save Metadata

↓

Save Outbox Event

If Outbox contains : VIDEO_UPLOADED and Status = PENDING then Then every few seconds

Outbox Scheduler

↓

Find Pending Events

↓

Send Kafka

↓

Mark Event = SENT

Even if Kafka is down for one hour, Nothing is lost. Outbox purpose is Never lose an event even if Kafka is unavailable.



Concept 2 :

Distributed Lock REDIS : Suppose tomorrow application grows

And we have multiple Processor for processing video

Processing Service 1 -> Kafka topic = video-upload

Processing Service 2 -> Kafka topic = video-upload

Processing Service 3 -> Kafka topic = video-upload

Processing Service 4 -> Kafka topic = video-upload


All consume the same Kafka topic = video-upload

Imagine Kafka accidentally delivers the same event twice.


VIDEO123

↓

Worker 1

Worker 2

Both worker will start working and Generating thumbnail, Generating 720p, Generating 1080p etc and Both upload files.


Redis Lock prevents this :

Worker 1 asks Redis - Can I process VIDEO123 ?

Redis says - YES Lock created.

Worker 2 asks Redis - Can I process VIDEO123 ?

Redis replies - NO Already processing.

Worker 2 simply exits.

Only one worker processes the video and Only one server can work on one video at one time.

